
## Getting Involved

I am acutely aware that as a professionally trained Accountant I may have used some conventions, definitions and styles that while seemingly obvious to me, might not be so clear to another developer. I would therefore welcome and greatly appreciate any feedback on the ease of use of the package so I can make it more useful to as many people as possible.


## Contributing

1. Fork it
2. Create your feature branch (`git checkout -b feature/fooBar`)
3. Set up the environment (this project uses [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), not poetry):

   ```bash
   uv sync --all-groups
   uv run pre-commit install
   ```

4. Write tests for the feature
5. Verify — the pre-commit hook runs the same gate as CI:

   ```bash
   uv run ruff format --check .   # must stay clean
   uv run ruff check .            # must stay clean
   uv run pytest
   ```

6. Commit your changes (`git commit -am 'Add some fooBar'`)
7. Push to the branch (`git push origin feature/fooBar`)
8. Create a new Pull Request

See `AGENTS.md` for architecture notes and testing quirks.
